    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Malt used in Brewing, Malting & Distilling: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 610"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MALT: (GER. Maly. DU. Mout. DA. and SW. Malt. FR. Mal, Blégermé. IT. Malto. SP. Cebada retonada ó entallecida. RUS. Solod. POL. Slod. LAT. Malum.) is, correctly, any corn prepared after a particular manner, for brewing the various kinds of beer; but in its general acceptance is applied only to barley so prepared.—Before we proceed to state the method of maki..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
